In article <ABRAHAM.93May21013458@loke.iesd.auc.dk>, abraham@research.att.com (Per Abrahamsen) writes:
>- Let wands of polymorph use one charge for each item or monster being
>polymorphed.

Actually, I'd suggest just not allowing polymorph to work on items. Or if
it must, then only to allow the intrinsic magic in an item to stay constant.
So that a +1 sword can become a +1 axe, but not a +3 club. Blessed and
cursed features remain so, and mundane items remain mundane. But it might
be possible for broken items to be repaired this way.

>- Let intrinsic protections have a (long) time-out.

I'd hope that intrinsic protections that came with a profession would
be permanent. Otherwise it could get really nasty. Also make sure that
there are ways of renewing protections on lower levels.

>- Make it impossible to get a named weapon from the Gods.

No, I figure that the whole point of gods was to bestow gifts if you've been
a good worshipper. There aren't that many routes to getting a weapon, this
method can be one of the reliable ways.

One thing I'd like to see is a guaranteed altar of the proper alignment
somewhere on the first few levels, somewhere between 1-8. So characters
can build up piety before going on a Quest.

>- Make intelligent monsters immune to conflict.

Or make it so that players can be vulnerable to a monster wearing a ring
of combat. :)
